      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "REASONS FOR NON-PHARMACOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT: Non-pharmacological management has the potential to reverse mild hypertension, to enhance effects of antihypertensive drugs, and to diminish fatal and non-fatal heart attack and stroke rates."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "EFFECTIVE MEASURES",
          "content": "For lowering blood pressure, weight control, alcohol moderation, salt restriction and exercise appear the most effective. Smoking cessation, and diets low in total and saturated fats and rich in fish, fruit and vegetables are also likely to substantially reduce atherosclerotic and thrombotic disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Advice on non-pharmacological management needs to be targeted appropriately for individuals and populations with widely varying behaviours which put them at risk of hypertension and its complications."
        }
      ]},
